#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:57
msgid ""
"image:skaven/logo.webp[width=120,height=108,float=\"right\"] Skaven are "
"neither rats nor human but a vile combination of the two races. The origins "
"of the Skaven are not known for certain. It is likely they were mutated at "
"the dawn of the Age of Chaos when powerful waves of magic swamped the "
"world.  Millions of tons of magically energised material were hurled over "
"the planet in the form of meteorites. Some of these were huge boulders as "
"big as a house but most were much smaller down to the finest particles of "
"dust that fell to earth and polluted the ground with magical energy. "
"Creatures that breathed the dust or strayed within the radiating power of "
"the larger stones became mutated into the most horrible monsters. The Skaven "
"may well have mutated from ordinary vermin as a result of consuming this "
"corrupting material – or ‘warpstone’ as they call it. Even today the Skaven "
"crave warpstone. Even minute traces of warpstone would kill most creatures "
"but for Skaven it is a potent stimulant and one that confers great powers "
"upon their sorcerers. It also destroys and mutates Skaven and drives them "
"insane – but such is its hold over the whole race that they delve for it "
"beneath the earth wherever it may be found."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:69
msgid ""
"Like ordinary rats Skaven abhor the daylight and avoid open places. They dig "
"tunnels beneath the earth, often taking over old Dwarf mines and Goblin "
"burrows. Though few suspect their presence they live below the cities of men "
"in the sewers and cellars and amongst ruins, emerging only at night to prey "
"upon vagrants and other unfortunates. Over the centuries the Skaven have "
"constructed thousands of miles of tunnels and huge city-sized nests so that "
"the whole planet is riddled with their workings. Even the mines of the "
"Dwarfs are undermined by the underworld of the Skaven and the two races have "
"fought many battles beneath the earth."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:83
msgid ""
"The Skaven thrive upon decay and corruption but their society is highly "
"stratified from the highest Lords of Decay to the most lowly Skaven slaves. "
"They live as large extended groups called Clans of which there are a great "
"many. The most powerful Clans rule the rest and they in turn are ruled over "
"by the Council of Thirteen whose members are the dreaded Lords of Decay. It "
"is this council that directs the Skaven’s attempts to overthrow the races of "
"the Overworld. The ordinary Clans are made up of many thousands of Skaven "
"warriors and slaves and very little else but some Clans have developed "
"special skills. These include Clan Pestilens whose rulers have developed a "
"form of germ warfare, spreading pestilence and corruption by means of "
"noxious vapours and poisons."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:95
msgid ""
"Clan Eshin is the master of subterfuge whose agents scuttle over the "
"rooftops of human cities on their secret missions of sabotage and "
"intelligence gathering. Clan Moulder’s sorcerers have become the masters of "
"mutating magic and have created many vile monsters by feeding them warpstone "
"– their most successful creations are the Rat Ogres – gigantic Skaven "
"monstrosities many times the size of an ordinary Skaven. Clan Skryre is "
"famed for its machineries that blend sorcery and an advanced science far "
"beyond the understanding of mere humans. Most powerful of all are the Grey "
"Seers the supreme sorcerers of the Skaven Race."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:100
#, no-wrap
msgid "Skaven army selector"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:105
#, no-wrap
msgid "include::partial$skaven.tsv[]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:113
#, no-wrap
msgid "Strength in Numbers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:115
msgid ""
"Brigades may be of any size and are not restricted to the normal four unit "
"maximum."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:116
#, no-wrap
msgid "Vermintide"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:123
msgid ""
"Skaven units that win a round of combat can choose to pursue retreating "
"enemy units regardless of troop type. Any Skaven units (including artillery) "
"can pursue any enemy units (including flyers, cavalry and chariots). "
"Although allowed to pursue regardless of enemy troop type, Skaven are still "
"constrained by terrain and fortified status the same as other armies – e.g. "
"they cannot pursue if fortified."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:124
#, no-wrap
msgid "Under the Lash"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:129
msgid ""
"All Skaven characters have a Command range of 20cm whether General, Heroes "
"or Wizards. Even Skaven Generals have a Command range of 20cm. Skaven are "
"very good at directing their underlings – but only so long as they remain "
"close at hand. We call it ‘under the lash’."
msgstr ""

#. 4: Paragraph breaks added
#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:137
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[jezzails,†1]]1. Jezzails"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:141
msgid ""
"Count enemy armour values as one worse than normal when shot by a jezzail. "
"So, for example, an armour value of 3+ counts as 4+, 5+ counts as 6+, and 6+ "
"can’t save against a Jezzail."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:142
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[plague-monks,†2]]2. Plague Monks"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:148
msgid ""
"A unit of Plague Monks will always use its initiative to charge an enemy if "
"possible and can’t be given orders instead. They will never use their "
"initiative to evade.  They can’t be driven back by shooting and never roll "
"for drive backs. If victorious in combat they must pursue or advance where "
"possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:151
msgid ""
"Plague Monks are unaffected by enemies that cause terror in combat, they do "
"not suffer the usual −1 Attack modifier."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:152
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[rat-swarms,†3]]3. Rat Swarms"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:154
msgid ""
"Rat Swarms cannot be driven back by shooting and do not roll for drive backs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:159
msgid ""
"A Rat Swarm stand cannot be supported by other kinds of infantry – only by "
"other Rat Swarm stands. Note, however, that Rat Swarms can support other "
"kinds of infantry as normal."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:162
msgid "A Rat Swarm cannot be given magic items."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:163
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[gutter-runners,†4]]4. Gutter Runners"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:167
msgid ""
"Skaven characters may ignore the Under the Lash rule when issuing orders to "
"Gutter Runners. Treat the character as having the normal command range for "
"their type."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:177
msgid ""
"Once deployed, orders can be given to the unit by the same character that "
"gave the infiltration order, [.edit]#ignoring the Under the Lash rule as "
"usual for Gutter Runners#."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:180
msgid "Gutter Runners don’t suffer the −1 Command penalty for Dense Terrain."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:181
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[warp-lightning-cannon,†5]]5. Warp Lightning Cannon"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:184
msgid ""
"The Warp Lightning Cannon follows the rules for xref:rules:artillery-and-"
"machines.adoc#elven-bolt-thrower[Elven Bolt Throwers] in the Rulebook, but "
"they can move up to 20cm. A half pace move is 10cm."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:189
msgid ""
"When making a shooting attack, any roll of double 1s to hit will cause the "
"Warp Lightning Cannon unit to become confused. This includes stand and shoot "
"attacks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:190
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[doom-wheel,†6]]6. Doom Wheel"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:195
msgid ""
"When the Doom Wheel charges against targets in the open it receives D6 bonus "
"Attacks in addition to the normal +1 Attack for charging. Note that this "
"bonus applies only when charging – not during pursuits, advances or when the "
"Doom Wheel is charged itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:197
msgid "The Doom Wheel has a move of 20cm and causes terror."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:198
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[screaming-bell,†7]]7. Screaming Bell"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:206
msgid ""
"A Screaming Bell is a gargantuan device and therefore it uses a 40 × 60mm "
"base, with the short edge being the front. It cannot move of its own accord "
"– but relies upon the great mass of Skaven to push it forward. The Screaming "
"Bell can therefore only move in the Command phase if it forms a brigade with "
"one or more infantry units. It can then move 20cm at infantry pace. It "
"cannot move using initiative and cannot be driven back by shooting and does "
"not roll for drive backs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:213
msgid ""
"In combat it is automatically destroyed if forced to retreat but will "
"pursue, advance and fall back so long as it is touching a Skaven infantry "
"unit at the start and end of its move: otherwise it cannot pursue, advance "
"or fall back as it is unable to move of its own accord."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:218
msgid ""
"All Skaven units touching the Screaming Bell are unaffected by the usual "
"penalty for Terror whilst they remain so. In addition, any Skaven Hero or "
"Warlock within 30cm of the Screaming Bell adds +1 to their Command value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:222
msgid ""
"Any enemy character within 30cm of the Screaming Bell deducts −1 from their "
"Command value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:225
msgid ""
"A Skaven army can only ever include a maximum of 1 Screaming Bell no matter "
"how large."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:226
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[grey-seer,†8]]8. Grey Seer"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:229
msgid ""
"The Grey Seer is the army’s General and can use Skaven magic in the same "
"manner as a Warlock and can be given a magic item restricted to either a "
"General or a Wizard."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:230
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[rat-ogre-bodyguard,†9]]9. Rat Ogre Bodyguard"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:233
msgid ""
"The Grey Seer, Heroes and Warlocks can have a Rat Ogre Bodyguard. A "
"character with a bodyguard adds +1 to his Attacks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:238
#, no-wrap
msgid "Skaven spells"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:241
#, no-wrap
msgid "Wither"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:247
msgid ""
"_Chanting a vile curse, the caster inflicts a wasting, shrinking sickness on "
"the enemy._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:256
#, no-wrap
msgid "Warp Lightning"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:262
msgid ""
"_An arc of pure warp energy strikes the foe wreaking strange changes, "
"melting flesh and twisting bone into monstrous forms._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:271
msgid ""
"Warp Lightning is treated like three ordinary shooting attacks except that "
"armour has no effect (all targets count as having no armour). A unit can be "
"driven back by Warp Lightning as with ordinary shooting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:273
#, no-wrap
msgid "Death Frenzy"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:280
msgid ""
"_The Skaven screams a blasphemous litany to the Horned Rat driving the "
"Skaven masses into a frenzy of warpdust fuelled destruction._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:284
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast upon a friendly unit that is engaged in combat and "
"which is within range. The Wizard does not have to be able to see the target "
"to cast the spell."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:300
msgid ""
"The unit gains bonus Death Frenzy attacks for the following combat phase. To "
"determine the number of bonus attacks roll one D6 at a time and add the "
"results together. The player can roll as many D6 as he wishes up to a "
"maximum of 1 per stand in the unit. The player always rolls one dice at a "
"time and can decide to stop at any point. However – if the player rolls a "
"second or subsequent dice and scores the same value as any previously rolled "
"dice, then the total Death Frenzy attacks are directed against the targeted "
"unit instead of its enemy. Death Frenzy attacks that rebound in this way are "
"struck only once in the first round of combat: they are not struck each "
"round."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:304
msgid ""
"Example, 1 + 4 + 6 = 11 extra attacks for the Skaven unit each round. "
"1 + 4 + 1 = 6 Attacks upon the Skaven unit in the first round."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:306
#, no-wrap
msgid "Plague"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:314
msgid ""
"_A swirling could of virulence envelopes the enemy troops causing their "
"bodies to erupt in pustules, their skins to split apart with running sores, "
"their joints to swell with buboes and their hair to crawl with lice and "
"fleas._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:318
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast on any unengaged enemy unit within range regardless "
"of whether the Wizard can see it or not. The spell cannot be cast on a unit "
"engaged in combat."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:322
msgid ""
"The unit suffers six attacks worked out in the usual way. A unit cannot be "
"driven back by Plague (the vile Plague erupts from within!)."
msgstr ""
